{"nodes": [{"id": "demo_readme_in_browser_demo", "label": "In-browser demo README (Acme Robotics)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://alayparikh.github.io/prod-grade-rag-assistant/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "demo_readme_ingest_query_split", "label": "Ingest in CI (Python) / query in browser (JavaScript) split", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "How it is split", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ingest runs once per deploy in CI with the real Python pipeline; the query path runs per question in the browser, so there is no server, no API key and nothing billable."}, {"id": "demo_readme_index_json_handoff", "label": "index.json hand-off (chunks, embeddings, pipeline constants)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "How it is split", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pipeline constants (k, fusion constant, rerank top-N, score cutoff) are read from the Python source so the two halves never hold different numbers."}, {"id": "demo_readme_browser_query_path", "label": "Browser query path (embed, meaning search, BM25, RRF, rerank, cutoff)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "The query path, step by step", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Uses all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2 via Transformers.js; BM25 uses the same tokenizer and constants as the Python FTS5 index; cutoff of -6 was calibrated on this corpus (answers score about -4 to +8, unrelated about -11)."}, {"id": "demo_readme_role_switch", "label": "Search as role switch (Admin / Engineer / HR / Contractor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "The interactive parts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "search.js drops files a role cannot open before retrieval, as the Python group filter does; a blocked file gets the same 'not covered' message as a missing one so its existence does not leak."}, {"id": "demo_readme_failure_cases", "label": "Where company search breaks (live failure cases)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "The interactive parts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 'What just happened' text is computed from each run's actual rankings, never written in advance."}, {"id": "demo_readme_pipeline_xray", "label": "Pipeline X-ray (four ranked lists side by side)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "The interactive parts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "demo_readme_privacy_meter", "label": "Requests since the models loaded (PerformanceObserver privacy meter)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "The interactive parts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "demo_readme_orders_pattern_translator", "label": "Orders pattern translator (nine parameterized SQL templates)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Ask the orders", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With no language model, the question is matched to one of nine query types by embedding similarity and values fill a parameterized template, so nothing typed becomes SQL text. Below similarity 0.45 it declines rather than guess. 'My orders' asks which customer rather than matching the nearest list."}, {"id": "demo_readme_per_role_sql_views", "label": "Per-role SQL views (prices hidden, West region only, no access)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Ask the orders", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "demo_readme_agent_chat", "label": "Demo agent chat panel (docked bottom-right, own role switch)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Ask the agent", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The page calls no model, so a question with a saved run replays it and any other question runs live with fixed steps. The panel's role switch is separate from the page's 'Search as'."}, {"id": "demo_readme_back_and_forth_rule", "label": "Back-and-forth rule (short reply joined to the asked-back question)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Ask the agent", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A reply of at most 8 words that is not itself a question completes the question the agent asked back about; that is the only context carried between messages since there is no model."}, {"id": "demo_readme_live_runs", "label": "Live runs (liverun.js: SQL templates then policy search, no model)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Ask the agent", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The answer is the translator's sentence plus the top passage of each search (at most 3 hold-reason searches), so it says nothing the steps did not return."}, {"id": "demo_readme_saved_runs", "label": "Saved agent runs (agent.json built by agent_runs.py, scripted by agent_examples.yaml)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Saved runs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tools, guards, role views and retrieval are real; only the model's step choice and answer wording are scripted. The build fails if a scripted answer claims more than its steps returned or holds something its role may not see. The --live path that records the real agent has not been run yet."}, {"id": "demo_readme_staleness_fingerprint", "label": "Staleness fingerprint (agent_runs.py --check)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Saved runs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "agent.json stores a fingerprint of fixtures, prompts, tool definitions, model, questions, roles and example script, recomputed on every deploy with no API call."}, {"id": "demo_readme_typed_question_matching", "label": "Typed question matching (0.8 similarity + matching numbers)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Saved runs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rewordings scored 0.60-0.93 and look-alikes up to 0.77, so no threshold separates them; the page uses 0.8 and also requires numbers in both questions to match, and one order never matches many. 8 of 14 test rewordings match a saved run; the rest run live."}, {"id": "demo_readme_roles_illustration", "label": "Demo roles are an illustration, not security", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Saved runs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On a static page every run ships with the page, so the role switch only replays the run made for that role; real enforcement lives in the full app's database and file server."}, {"id": "demo_readme_check_search", "label": "check_search.mjs browser check (golden set, 64 agent checks, 18 order cases)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "demo/README.md", "source_location": "Files", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "demo_readme_limitations", "label": "What 